Unapplied activation artifact: joined broker serialization primitives
====================================================================

Apply after broker-runtime-activation.patch, before the shared session codec
extraction (Frame/MessageAssembler/Sending::next_frame/mark_sent visibility).
No active source has been changed. Add mod broker_spool in the runtime activation
module list. This patch alone does not link or compile the staged broker.

Payload::from_parts accepts only private fully serialized spools whose worker was
joined. Sending::from_payload performs header/control validation and opens its
bounded reader without serializing or spawning a task. The existing ordinary
Sending::new still validates headers before using its original serializer;
broker_writer never calls it. Both constructors use the same header validator.
The subsequent next_frame extraction must retain/await each bounded spool read;
it must not race that read against cancellation or detach its Tokio file work.

